<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<object type="traktor.mcp.SkillAsset">
	<name>create-animated-character</name>
	<description>Build a skinned, animated character entity (skeleton, weights, clips, state graph, CharacterComponent).</description>
	<whenToUse><![CDATA[Asked to create a playable/animated character or creature with a skeleton and animations. To EDIT or extend an existing rig instead — add joints (forearms, hands, feet), re-skin part of the mesh, or add joints to existing animation takes — use the edit-skinned-rig skill.]]></whenToUse>
	<body><![CDATA[# Create a skinned, animated character entity

Build a skinned character ("{{name}}", colour "{{color}}", ~{{height}} m tall) with a skeleton, vertex weights, animation clips, an optional Idle↔Walk state graph, and a physics `CharacterComponent`.

## Pipeline
model `.tmd` (geometry + joints + weights + animations) → `SkeletonAsset` + one `AnimationAsset` per clip → runtime Skeleton/Animation. Entity = `SkeletonComponentData` + `AnimatedMeshComponentData` + `CharacterComponentData` (+ a state-graph pose controller).

## Steps
1. **One model carries geometry, skeleton and animations**: call `create_mesh_from_geometry` with
   - `meshType: "skinned"`;
   - `joints`: `[{name, parent (index; -1 = root), translation (LOCAL = global − parent-global), rotation [0,0,0,1], length}]`, **listed parent before child**;
   - `jointIndices`: per-position joint index (rigid single-bone bind, weight 1);
   - `animations`: `[{name, keyframes:[{time, pose:[[tx,ty,tz,qx,qy,qz,qw] × jointCount]}]}]`;
   - `material`, `triangulate: true`. The returned guid is stable across re-runs.
2. **Colour**. There is no colour argument. The generated material shader uses the model material's colour, so set it after creating the mesh:
   - `model_open {meshAsset}`
   - `model_edit {handle, edits:[{op:"setMaterials", values:[{name:"<material>", color:[r,g,b,1]}]}]}`
   - `model_save {handle, overwriteSource:true}`

   Re-running `create_mesh_from_geometry` resets the colour. For textures use `maps:{diffuse:""}` + `texCoords` + `materialTextures` (see *create-mesh-from-geometry*). For a custom look use `materialShaders` (see *shader-graph-authoring*).
3. `build_asset` the mesh.
4. **Animation assets**:
   - One `traktor.animation.SkeletonAsset` (`fileName` → the `.tmd`).
   - One `traktor.animation.AnimationAsset` per clip (`fileName` → `.tmd`, `take` = clip name; empty `take` = clip 0).
   - `build_asset` each.
5. **Entity components**:
   - `traktor.animation.SkeletonComponentData { skeleton: <SkeletonAsset guid>, poseController }`
   - `traktor.animation.AnimatedMeshComponentData { mesh: <mesh guid> }`
   - `traktor.physics.CharacterComponentData`:
     - `radius`, `height`, `step`;
     - `jumpImpulse`: vertical velocity added on jump; the default 1 is a ~5 cm hop, ~5 gives ~1.4 m;
     - `maxVelocity`: caps horizontal speed, default 2 m/s;
     - **`traceInclude`: the collision group(s) of the ground**, e.g. Default `{F9805131-50C2-504C-9421-13C99E44616C}`.
6. **Idle/Walk state graph** (optional), a `traktor.animation.StateGraph` with:
   - `StateNodeAnimation` states (`version="2"`):
     - `animations` = list of AnimationAsset guids; the compiler emits one runtime state per animation, so the graph picks one at random each time the state is entered;
     - `loopDuration` = the cross fade used by the generated looping transitions.
   - `StateTransition`s: `condition` string (leading `!` inverts), `moment` = "Immediately".
   - `rootState`.

   `create_instance` the StateGraph first, then author it with **`import_instance_from_xml`** (it only replaces an existing instance; see Gotchas). `build_asset` → `RtStateGraph`. Point the pose controller at it: `traktor.animation.AnimationGraphPoseControllerData { stateGraph: <StateGraph guid> }`.

## Gotchas (hard-won)
- **Winding**: a face is front-facing when `cross(p2−p0, p1−p0)` points outward (counter-clockwise seen from outside in Traktor's left-handed view). Auto-orient every quad: if `dot(cross(p1−p0, p2−p0), outwardNormal) > 0`, reverse the vertex order.
- **Weights**: the skinned converter keeps the top-4 influences and normalizes them (a single-bone vertex is left unnormalized = 1). Use rigid single-bone binds unless you need blending.
- **Give every joint a value in every keyframe**: its bind local transform if it doesn't move. A joint left out of *every* keyframe keeps its bind offset. A joint keyed in only *some* keyframes collapses onto its parent in the frames where it is missing.
- **`AnimationAsset.removeTranslation` defaults to true**: joint 0's forward (Z) travel is stripped into root motion, which only `SkeletonComponent:consumeRootMotion` applies. Author walk clips in place; the CharacterComponent does the moving.
- **Drive the graph from script with `poseController:setParameterValue(name, bool)`**; `setState(...)` is a no-op stub. For script setup (`import(traktor)`, passing component types directly to `getComponent`), see the *traktor-lua-scripting* skill.
- A `"moving"` transition and a `"!moving"` transition share one boolean parameter `moving`.
- The editor state-graph view relies on shared object identity (`ref=` ids). Only `import_instance_from_xml` produces those; `set_instance_member` leaves the graph unwired.]]></body>
	<engineVersion/>
	<published>true</published>
	<parameters>
		<item type="traktor.mcp.SkillParameter">
			<name>name</name>
			<description>Entity/asset name</description>
			<defaultValue>Character</defaultValue>
		</item>
		<item type="traktor.mcp.SkillParameter">
			<name>color</name>
			<description>Body colour</description>
			<defaultValue>yellow</defaultValue>
		</item>
		<item type="traktor.mcp.SkillParameter">
			<name>height</name>
			<description>Approx height in metres</description>
			<defaultValue>1.85</defaultValue>
		</item>
	</parameters>
</object>
